1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,780
We're setting up a new location: the Indirect Material Inspection station.

2
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:13,199
One workbench, one material cart, one magnifying lamp, a notebook, and seats for 1 or 2 operators.

3
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:20,251
The bench is 1550 mm long, 750 deep, and 2200 tall.

4
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:29,329
A blue, powder-coated steel frame carries a 30 mm worktop, with a white ESD dissipative laminate.

5
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:35,430
Below, a lower shelf in the same laminate, its edge protected by a stainless steel angle.

6
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:41,880
On the left, a 2-level stainless steel cart brings material in, and takes it back when the check is done.

7
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:46,046
Beside it, a black ESD bin for waste, with a push lid.

8
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:55,957
The LED panel reaches 700 mm forward, on angled brackets, lighting the whole worktop.

9
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:04,180
At the left rear corner, an 8× ESD magnifying lamp swings over the center, for close visual checks.

10
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:10,530
Above, a full-length cabinet, with one wide door and a key lock, keeps the measuring tools secure.

11
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:17,851
Inside: digital verniers, a micrometer on its stand, a thickness gauge, a tape measure, and a steel ruler.

12
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:23,437
Along the back, a 4-outlet power rail.

13
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:27,742
On the right side, a notebook computer.

14
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:36,607
Two blue ESD chairs, with foot rings and casters, seat 1 or 2 operators.

15
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:43,661
One location. Everything the inspector needs, within reach.
